  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "When a craft crashed on a mesa near the Archuleta ranch in New Mexico in 1948, it left a streak on the cliff that can still be seen today, Michels says. He tells this himself, drawing on a man named Scott Ramsey, whom he counts as a witness to the site. To Michels the mark is lasting physical evidence that something really came down there."
